# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# RDR-5, RDR-6 and RDR-8: page a long entry with F1, step back with
# Backspace, and leave by the far end. Since M5-E4d (#305) the page a
# player opens from the bar is a **full screen** — the same box the
# `Notes` listing is drawn in — so the give-back is the whole screen and
# not the roster's cells.
#
# **A single leg, and it has to be one.** It was a pair, and a pair
# cannot say anything about this any more, for `not-log-giveback.leg`'s
# own reason: the page covers the screen, so a rect that allowed it would
# allow everything and check nothing, and the composer that puts the
# screen back resets the command bar's highlight, so the frames after
# Escape differ from the seam-off run on the bar row however exact the
# give-back is (#234).
#
# So it says the two things a single leg can say, and they are stronger:
# each page holds still while it is up, and the screen before the reader
# opened is the screen after it closed.
about paging a long entry full-screen, and giving the screen back exactly
kind single
program START.EXE
store tests/visual/reader-store.txt
both code-wheel
# The code-wheel bypass is gated on the wheel itself (#115), and this run
# drives past the challenge, so it needs it. Pinned by digest because a
# document never enters this tree.
document 0db301aeac4d2ec1e63b409ca6d3c9d39c63381d6712ff2ce7edc0528c6586fd
seam journal
until 300000000
every 25

key A@7601
key Return@7651
key L@8951
key A@9201
# F1 opens the prompt — which stays in the panel, four digits and a
# caption — and Return opens the entry on the whole screen.
key F1@10600
key 3@10700
key Return@10800
# Forward, back, forward, and then out through the far end: the entry is
# two pages at thirty-eight columns by twenty rows, so the F1 on the
# second one is the way out rather than a third page.
key F1@11200
key Backspace@11600
key F1@12000
key F1@12400

rect bar 0,190,319,199

# Each page, holding still with nothing pressed.
same 10850-11175
same 11250-11575
same 11650-11975
same 12050-12375

# And the screen before the reader took it, back again after it: every
# pixel **except the bar row**, which is `not-log-giveback.leg`'s finding
# rather than a convenience — the give-back injects a space to make the
# menu-bar routine return and draw itself again, and the routine draws
# itself with the highlight at its first command.
equal 10600 12600 bar
